{
  "name": "exactly twenty assets",
  "description": "The asset cap is `>`, not `>=`: twenty is admitted by the table and the refusal vector next door carries twenty-one. This is a statement about the **table**, not about a request anyone can make - twenty minimal batteries are a 4 336-byte blob and the transport's 4 096-byte cap refuses them, so the byte cap is the binding one in practice. Both are kept, because the byte cap is a property of the encoding and the asset cap is a property of the model, and a future variant with shorter fields would move which one bites first.",
